{
  "id": "apltyxi",
  "title": "Electrical Measurements",
  "order": 8,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6pjfbp8",
      "content": "<strong>CHAPTER 8 — ELECTRICAL MEASUREMENTS</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c4bvr5b",
      "content": "Electrical measurements are critical in PSU examinations, particularly for BEL, MDL, and measurement-focused PSU exams. Instruments are classified by their operating principle. Understanding how each instrument works, what it measures, and its limitations is essential."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "u80kx5s",
      "content": "<strong>8.1  Classification of Indicating Instruments</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "xgaf11z",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Instrument Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Principle</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Measures</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Waveform</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Key Property</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>PMMC (Permanent Magnet Moving Coil)</p>",
            "<p>Interaction of permanent magnet field with coil current</p>",
            "<p>DC current and voltage only</p>",
            "<p>DC only</p>",
            "<p>High accuracy; uniform scale; damped by eddy currents</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Moving Iron (MI)</p>",
            "<p>Force on iron piece in coil's magnetic field</p>",
            "<p>AC and DC (reads RMS)</p>",
            "<p>AC &amp; DC</p>",
            "<p>Cheap; robust; scale not uniform; widely used in industry</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Electrodynamometer</p>",
            "<p>Interaction between two coil fields</p>",
            "<p>Power (wattmeter); AC/DC</p>",
            "<p>AC &amp; DC</p>",
            "<p>Wattmeter; power factor meter; transfer instrument</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Induction type</p>",
            "<p>Induction in a disc (Ferraris principle)</p>",
            "<p>Energy (kWh) — energy meters</p>",
            "<p>AC only</p>",
            "<p>Used in energy metering; creep error possible</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Rectifier type</p>",
            "<p>PMMC + rectifier (diodes)</p>",
            "<p>AC (reads mean; calibrated for RMS)</p>",
            "<p>AC via rectifier</p>",
            "<p>Good sensitivity; frequency error possible</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Thermocouple type</p>",
            "<p>Heat generated by I²R; EMF produced</p>",
            "<p>True RMS of AC</p>",
            "<p>Any waveform</p>",
            "<p>True RMS; frequency independent; for high frequency</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "3xcju7d",
      "content": "<strong>8.2  Current Transformer (CT) &amp; Potential Transformer (PT)</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "by9dng5",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Feature</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Current Transformer (CT)</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Potential Transformer (PT)</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Connection</p>",
            "<p>Series with circuit (primary carries line current)</p>",
            "<p>Shunt (parallel) with circuit</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Purpose</p>",
            "<p>Steps down high current for measurement</p>",
            "<p>Steps down high voltage for measurement</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Secondary burden</p>",
            "<p>Connected to ammeter (low impedance)</p>",
            "<p>Connected to voltmeter (high impedance)</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Critical rule</p>",
            "<p>Secondary MUST NEVER be open-circuited (high voltage danger)</p>",
            "<p>Secondary MUST NEVER be short-circuited</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Standard secondary rating</p>",
            "<p>5A or 1A</p>",
            "<p>110V</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Accuracy classes</p>",
            "<p>0.1, 0.2, 0.5, 1, 3, 5</p>",
            "<p>0.1, 0.2, 0.5, 1, 3</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Error types</p>",
            "<p>Ratio error and phase angle error</p>",
            "<p>Ratio error and phase angle error</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Application</p>",
            "<p>Protective relays, energy meters, ammeters</p>",
            "<p>Voltmeters, protective relays, energy meters</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "x58qq4c",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>CRITICAL SAFETY: Opening the secondary of a CT while the primary is energised is extremely dangerous. The secondary voltage rises to very high values (dangerously high EMF) because there is no demagnetising effect of secondary current. Always short-circuit the CT secondary before opening the circuit.</strong></p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "97ygtwl",
      "content": "<strong>8.3  Wheatstone Bridge</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "43c944p",
      "content": "The Wheatstone Bridge is used to measure unknown resistance with high precision. It consists of four resistors in a diamond arrangement with a galvanometer across the middle."
    },
    {
      "id": "ekzp8p1",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Balance condition: P/Q = R/S   →   Unknown resistor S = QR/P</strong></p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "el8ve28",
      "content": "At balance, no current flows through the galvanometer. The bridge is most sensitive when all four arms have nearly equal resistance. For very low resistance measurement, Kelvin's Double Bridge is used (eliminates contact and lead resistance effects). For high resistance, Megohmmeter is used."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1efx51t",
      "content": "<strong>8.4  Measurement of Power</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "svboc5j",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Method</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Applicable To</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Formula/Connection</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Notes</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Single wattmeter</p>",
            "<p>Single-phase AC; balanced 3-phase</p>",
            "<p>Direct reading in watts</p>",
            "<p>One wattmeter measures P = VI cosφ</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Two wattmeter method</p>",
            "<p>3-phase (balanced or unbalanced)</p>",
            "<p>P = W₁ + W₂; tanφ = √3(W₁−W₂)/(W₁+W₂)</p>",
            "<p>Most common for 3-phase power measurement</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Three wattmeter method</p>",
            "<p>3-phase 4-wire unbalanced</p>",
            "<p>P = W₁ + W₂ + W₃</p>",
            "<p>Each wattmeter measures one phase</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Digital power meter</p>",
            "<p>Any waveform</p>",
            "<p>Multiplies instantaneous V and I, integrates</p>",
            "<p>True power measurement; handles harmonics</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2fl0l9r",
      "content": "<strong>8.5  Practice MCQs — Measurements</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5jcy7f6",
      "content": "<strong>Q1.  </strong>A PMMC instrument can measure:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "6bx0z32",
      "content": "        (A)  AC only"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "m759niv",
      "content": "        (B)  DC only"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2sid1nb",
      "content": "        (C)  Both AC and DC"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "4yper66",
      "content": "        (D)  True RMS of AC"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l5wbm93",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(B)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6al3q76",
      "content": "<strong>Q2.  </strong>The current transformer (CT) secondary should never be:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "z80xykt",
      "content": "        (A)  Short-circuited"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hsbgpbq",
      "content": "        (B)  Open-circuited"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "cxo6gkr",
      "content": "        (C)  Connected to ammeter"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "71gspu7",
      "content": "        (D)  Earthed"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "tilf636",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(B)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "pakc9eq",
      "content": "<strong>Q3.  </strong>An induction type energy meter measures:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vbsjh2u",
      "content": "        (A)  Power (Watts)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "o6feonf",
      "content": "        (B)  Power factor"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ubri6ti",
      "content": "        (C)  Energy (kWh)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "apw840v",
      "content": "        (D)  Current (Amperes)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hlecfpx",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(C)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "eyczt4e",
      "content": "<strong>Q4.  </strong>In Wheatstone bridge balance condition (P/Q = R/S), unknown S equals:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5lot93p",
      "content": "        (A)  PQ/R"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "37r5h0i",
      "content": "        (B)  QR/P"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ua3i7fb",
      "content": "        (C)  PR/Q"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ggapbi5",
      "content": "        (D)  PQR"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "q9svixb",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(B)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "kdjtxcc",
      "content": "<strong>Q5.  </strong>The two-wattmeter method for 3-phase power gives tanφ =:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0ehdsvd",
      "content": "        (A)  (W₁+W₂)/(W₁−W₂)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "67115m3",
      "content": "        (B)  √3(W₁−W₂)/(W₁+W₂)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "89ub6gv",
      "content": "        (C)  (W₁−W₂)/√3"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "g4joohm",
      "content": "        (D)  √3(W₁+W₂)/(W₁−W₂)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "vmc42jd",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(B)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oj7aukz",
      "content": "<strong>Q6.  </strong>Moving Iron instruments measure:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "1pm8bis",
      "content": "        (A)  Average value of AC"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "lihfxjm",
      "content": "        (B)  Peak value of AC"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4lc5f3q",
      "content": "        (C)  RMS value of AC and DC"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "p5e7g68",
      "content": "        (D)  Instantaneous value"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "imfxtlx",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(C)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ky9r2dg",
      "content": "<strong>Q7.  </strong>Creep error in an energy meter is due to:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "ebr2s4l",
      "content": "        (A)  Overloading"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "nhtfmf7",
      "content": "        (B)  Disc rotating with no load due to voltage"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "r673fs6",
      "content": "        (C)  Incorrect calibration"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "xu3bb5i",
      "content": "        (D)  Temperature effects"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0hggcux",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(B)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7lxrrzy",
      "content": "<strong>Q8.  </strong>For measuring very low resistance, which bridge is used?"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8d2cab2",
      "content": "        (A)  Wheatstone bridge"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "0ll9d78",
      "content": "        (B)  Kelvin double bridge"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "8vgcjzn",
      "content": "        (C)  Hay bridge"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "k9nxpes",
      "content": "        (D)  Maxwell bridge"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "hsy1nhf",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(B)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g5fn7z7",
      "content": "<strong>Q9.  </strong>A dynamometer type instrument is used as:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mr05p40",
      "content": "        (A)  Voltmeter only"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "a0kn6cb",
      "content": "        (B)  Ammeter only"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "9wuycve",
      "content": "        (C)  Wattmeter"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "3az8qdl",
      "content": "        (D)  Energy meter"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "fsid17k",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(C)"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ewgzdxn",
      "content": "<strong>Q10.  </strong>The main advantage of PMMC over Moving Iron instrument is:"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "l4x7rw2",
      "content": "        (A)  Can measure AC"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "2nnbe9n",
      "content": "        (B)  Lower cost"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7qe89zs",
      "content": "        (C)  Uniform scale and higher accuracy"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "5jb1qgp",
      "content": "        (D)  Works at high frequencies"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "mxw6klg",
      "content": "<strong>Answer: </strong>(C)"
    }
  ],
  "enriched": true
}